(ned -- C REFERENCE TEACH, operator spec 2026-08-03.)
(NO MOTION. The operator jogs A to -45 and puts the tool tip where driving)
(toward the puck centre in +X would strike it; this button records that pose)
(as offsets from the puck centre so StartC and StartAC can replay it with no)
(operator input -- the 5x iteration cannot stop to ask.)

(The sideways offset dy is not just a position, it IS the scale factor of the)
(C measurement: dX = -2 * dy * sin phi. So it is checked, not assumed.)

(Stores: #3058 = dy off centre, #3060 = depth below the top, #3061 = X offset.)

o<cal_c_ref> sub
  #<cx>  = #1
  #<cy>  = #2
  #<top> = #3

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, SET C REF: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, SET C REF: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  (#5420-#5425 = current X Y Z A B C in the work frame)
  #<a_now> = #5423
  o10 if [ABS[#<a_now> + 45] GT 5.0]
    (abort, SET C REF: A is at #<a_now> deg - jog A to -45 first, then press SET C REF.)
  o10 endif

  #<dx_off> = [#5420 - #<cx>]
  #<dy_off> = [#5421 - #<cy>]
  #<depth>  = [#<top> - #5422]

  o20 if [ABS[#<dy_off>] LT 1.0]
    (abort, SET C REF: the tip is within 1 mm of centre in Y. That offset IS the scale factor of the C measurement so it cannot be near zero - jog sideways as the -45 tilt puts it.)
  o20 endif
  o30 if [#<depth> LE 0]
    (abort, SET C REF: the tip is at or above the puck top - jog DOWN so that driving toward centre would strike the puck.)
  o30 endif
  o40 if [#<dx_off> GE 0]
    (abort, SET C REF: the tip is not in FRONT of the puck - it must sit at negative X of centre so the probe drives toward centre in +X.)
  o40 endif

  #3061 = #<dx_off>
  #3058 = #<dy_off>
  #3060 = #<depth>
  #3059 = 0

  (PRINT, SET C REF stored: X offset #3061 mm, dy off centre #3058 mm, depth below top #3060 mm. StartC and StartAC now replay this automatically.)
  (DEBUG, SET C REF: dy #3058, depth #3060, xoff #3061)

o<cal_c_ref> endsub

M2 (end program)
